From: skrimix <skrimix.git@fastmail.org>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: wake on USB input changes

Plugging in a charger while suspended delivers a USB property
notification, but nothing wakes the system, so userspace only notices
the charger after another wake source. Report it as a hard wakeup event
on the USB supply, as the downstream battery charger driver does, so its
power/wakeup attribute controls it.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index f6b77405d..6c2721639 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -3689,6 +3689,14 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_notification(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 		break;
 	case NOTIF_USB_PROPERTY:
 		qcom_battmgr_pps_kick(battmgr);
+		/*
+		 * Wake from sleep on USB input changes such as plugging in a
+		 * charger, so that userspace can pick up the new charging state.
+		 * Controlled by the USB supply's power/wakeup attribute.
+		 */
+		pm_wakeup_dev_event(&battmgr->usb_psy->dev, 0, true);
 		power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
 		break;
 	case NOTIF_WLS_PROPERTY:
